    "body": "26 files, **\u22121,640 lines**. **No compiler can check any of this**, so the liveness\nargument matters more than the diff. Three commits, each using a progressively\nstronger test.\n\n## 1. Three whole stylesheets\n\n- **`assistant.css` (833 lines)** \u2014 every rule is scoped under `#assistant`, and\n  nothing renders `id=\"assistant\"`. The sidebar's HelpfulAssistant panel renders\n  `AgentView.view` (`Sidebar.re:340`), styled by `style/agent/*.css`, which is\n  where every class the agent UI actually uses (`send-button`,\n  `message-container`, `message-identifier`, `llm-identifier`, `dot1`, \u2026) is\n  defined. The only unscoped rules \u2014 `.llm-selector`/`.llm-label`/`.llm-dropdown`\n  \u2014 are unreferenced in source.\n- **`project.css` (315 lines)** \u2014 styles a projects/file-system UI that no longer\n  exists. All five ids and 18 of 20 classes have zero source references; the other\n  two are generic (`.cell`, `.icon`) matched only as descendants of the dead ids.\n- **`agent.css`** \u2014 empty file, imported nowhere.\n\n## 2. Individual rules, judged by source grep\n\n22 rule blocks across 9 stylesheets, 12 unreferenced icons, and\n`style/palette.html` (a design swatch page nothing links to and no dune rule\ncopies into the build).\n\nThe test is deliberately over-cautious. A selector counts as **live** if any of:\n\n- its name appears as a string literal anywhere in `src/` or `test/`;\n- **some literal is a prefix of it**, since classes get concatenated \u2014\n  `\"depth-\" ++ string_of_int n`, `\"agent-md-h\" ++ string_of_int level`,\n  `\"highlight-code-\" ++ c`, `\"slash-card-\" ++ kind`;\n- **its name appears as a bare OCaml token.** `Sort` and `cls` constructors reach\n  the DOM through `show`/`to_string` and never appear as a literal at all \u2014 that\n  is `.Mod`, `.Sig`, `.MPat`, `.Rul`, `.EmptyHole`, `.Single`. A naive\n  literals-only scan called all of those dead.\n\nThat took the candidate list from 72 names to 22, each then re-checked by hand for\nboth hyphenated and underscored spellings.\n\nA rule is removed only when **every** comma-separated selector is dead, judged by\nthe key (rightmost) compound: `.projector.probe .window-toggle` can only match an\nelement carrying `.window-toggle`, so it goes even though `.projector` is live.\nRules whose key compound is an element selector are left alone\n(`.step-back:hover span` survives) \u2014 which leaves a few orphans but cannot break\nanything.\n\n## 3. The stronger test: grep the compiled bundle\n\nIf a class name appears nowhere in the 11 MB `hazel.js`, no code path can put it\non an element, so any rule naming it is unreachable. Controls confirm the test\ndiscriminates rather than trivially passing: `projector` 108 hits, `probe` 256,\n`hsod` 9, `depth-` 4, `highlight-code-` 1, `agent-md-h` 3.\n\nTen classes still defined in CSS can never be emitted, and their rules go:\n`developer-notes-display`, `view-icon-button`, `deselected`, `call-cursor`,\n`click-kbd-pill`, `is-index`, `qr-when-unfocused`, `window-toggle`, `step-back`,\n`step-expand`. Nine are ones commit 2 deliberately spared for having an element\nkey selector \u2014 unreachable all the same, since nothing carries `.step-back`.\n\n**`call-cursor` is a correction.** Commit 2 kept it because `call_cursor` exists in\nsource \u2014 but that is a function name; the hyphenated class is never emitted. The\nsource-grep test was wrong there and the bundle test is right. That is the honest\nsummary of why there are two commits instead of one.\n\nWhere a rule mixed dead and live selectors, only the dead branches are dropped:\n`.prompt-display, .developer-notes-display` keeps `.prompt-display`. One such trim\ninitially took the rule's leading comment with it, because the dead branch was\nlisted first and carried the preceding trivia \u2014 restored.\n\n## Browser verification\n\nDone, and it covers all three commits: probe sidebar (including\n`#sample-focus-bar` with a focused sample, and probe hover cards with kbd badges),\nagent panel, agent main menu, nut menu, editor context menu, stepper (took a\nstep), tutorial mode (completed a step, checkmark renders), exercises mode with\ngrading reports, and the projectors slide. No console errors, no unstyled surfaces.\n\nIf you re-verify: **restart the browser rather than hard-reloading** \u2014 a stale Web\nWorker survives a reload and reports `EXN:TypeError reading '1'` from eval, which\nlooks like a real regression and is not.\n\n`licenses/Icons.md` is a blanket Noun Project attribution rather than per-icon, so\nremoving unused icons does not affect it.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
